<DocsLayout title="Plugin Development" section="plugins">
  <h1>Plugin Development</h1>

  <p>*ARRgh!'s source plugins are esbuild-bundled TypeScript modules that implement a simple HTTP API. The plugin host loads them and proxies requests from the Rust server.</p>

  <p><strong>Start from <a href="https://github.com/t2vi/arrgh-plugin-template" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">arrgh-plugin-template</a>.</strong> It wires in the <a href="https://github.com/t2vi/arrgh-plugin-sdk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">plugin SDK</a> (protocol types, <code>arrgh-plugin build</code>, contract tests) and includes CI plus a release workflow that publishes the bundle, its sha256 and the catalog entry.</p>

  <h2>Plugin protocol</h2>

  <p>A plugin exposes these endpoints over HTTP:</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>GET /info</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Plugin metadata — <code>id</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>version</code>, <code>content_types</code>, <code>default_explicit</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>GET /manga/:source_id/chapters</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Chapter list for a title</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>GET /chapter/:source_id/pages</code></td><td>Yes (comics)</td><td>Image URLs for a chapter</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>GET /chapter/:source_id/text</code></td><td>Yes (novels)</td><td>Markdown text for a novel chapter</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>Plugins are <strong>download-only</strong>. Search, covers, and metadata come from the discover fan-out authorities (MangaUpdates, AniList, MangaDex, NovelUpdates, WuxiaWorld, Royal Road, nhentai) — plugins do not need to implement <code>/search</code> or <code>/meta</code>.</p>

