  <h2>Distributing via the plugin index</h2>

  <p>Community plugins can be listed in the <a href="https://github.com/t2vi/arrgh/blob/main/plugin-index/index.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">plugin index</a> so users can browse and install them from Settings. Open a PR to add your plugin.</p>

  <p>An entry needs a <code>download_url</code> (the release's <code>.js</code> bundle), its <code>sha256</code> and the <code>protocol</code> version it was built for (currently <code>1</code>). The plugin host downloads the bundle, rejects it unless the checksum matches, and loads it without a restart. To ship a fix, publish a new release and bump <code>version</code>, <code>download_url</code> and <code>sha256</code> in the index. Admins then see an <strong>Update</strong> button, and <strong>Revert</strong> returns to the version bundled with *ARRgh.</p>
</DocsLayout>
